The luminosities of the positive and negative helicity collisions were kept as close to each other as possible. However, the luminosities varied between helicity states, and this difference was measured by the relative luminosity. For the asymmetry measurement, the relative luminosities were measured by looking at how many events occurred as measured by remnant particles hitting the BBC for the different helicity states.

